<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) Achieng saved Ksh <m>{30\,000}</m> in a SACCO account that pays simple interest. After <m>{3}</m> years the amount was Ksh <m>{37\,200}</m>. Find the rate of interest per annum.</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/> %  </p><p>(b) A chama lends Ksh <m>{14\,000}</m> at <m>{9}\%</m> per annum simple interest and receives Ksh <m>{5040}</m> interest. For how many years was the money lent?</p><p><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> years  </p><p>Give each answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The interest is the amount minus the principal: <m>I = {37\,200} - {30\,000} = {7200}</m>. Then</p><p><me>R = \frac{100I}{PT} = \frac{100 \times {7200}}{{30\,000} \times {3}} = {8}.</me></p><p>The rate is <m>{8}\%</m> per annum.</p><p>(b) <me>T = \frac{100I}{PR} = \frac{100 \times {5040}}{{14\,000} \times {9}} = {4}.</me></p><p>The money was lent for <m>{4}</m> years.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>8</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>